      "writtenOn": "2024-08-21T04:36:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Urg. This looks like it could break the way the Android stack does IPv6 on wifi, which would be unacceptable.\n\nThere may be other consequences as well.\n\nCan you explain what you plan to use this for, and what the design will look like? We are happy to have a meeting to discuss if that works for you.",
      "parentUuid": "bc1f9435_e1ced6ea",
      "revId": "16d994d752c02757c8d4eaf0bdd4bba043442c0c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "41925cd3_08bff16d",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 3371323
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-22T02:45:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We are using this IPVLAN driver to create virtual interfaces for actual physical interface, which can be used by apps. \nI shall try to supress that CONFIG_L3, and check if something breaks in functionality.\n\n\nKindly provide answers to my below queries:\n1. Can you please let me know, if I can enable this CONFIG_IPVLAN\u003dm and CONFIG_IF_TARGET_TTL\u003dm , inside vendor fragment file. Does fragment file overwrite the configs of gki_defconfig?\nKindly provide the documentation or steps to enable. I tried once, but it crashes on device. module gets compiled even through fragment file, but when i run command to use it, it gets crashed. \n\n2. I dont want to modify gki_defconfig for all those configs, kindly suggest how we can enable or disable the CONFIG if those CONFIG are not as per our need in gki_defconfig file. For example: if something is disabled in gki_defconfig, can I enable it for our use case. \n\n3. Can you maintain a separate gki_defconfig for all vendors?  I have seen some Qualcom CONFIG (CONFIG_**_QCOM_**) being merged in gki_defconfig and those CONFIG are not relevant for Samsung, now if we want to disable those configs, should we push the patches to Google?  But it is a kind of never-ending process, other vendors will keep adding their CONFIG in gki_defconfig, and Samsung will keep raising request to remove those.\nCan you please provide a solution for this?",
      "parentUuid": "82afe348_c5e41acf",
      "revId": "16d994d752c02757c8d4eaf0bdd4bba043442c0c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
